    "added_lines": [
      "- **Heavy runs go through simjob,** inside the host budget: anything using more than one core or running more than a few minutes. Never run them bare.",
      "- **A simjob refusal is a wait, not a stop.** Exit 75 means memory pressure or budget, and simjob's own documentation says \"try again later\". Retry the unchanged command, with the same resources, whenever admission permits, as often as it takes. This brief is your authority; do not file to ask. Never raise the resources or go around simjob."
    ],
    "current_minus_added_is_dispatched": true,
    "effect": "heavy runs go through simjob and a refusal is retried unchanged; this card's runs were moved onto simjob when the order and amendments were read"
  },
